  "known_gaps": [
    "No direct trial establishes the superiority of explicit training blocks for recreational runners training 3-4 times per week.",
    "No universal fixed block duration, cutback cadence, recipe starting dose, testing cadence, taper percentage, or interruption-return schedule is supported.",
    "Threshold and critical-speed methods are protocol/model dependent and not automatically interchangeable.",
    "Elite periodization and session density are descriptive and cannot be dose-transferred.",
    "Token estimates use a transparent character proxy because an exact model tokenizer was unavailable; measured characters and words are retained.",
    "The exact main-branch commit SHA was not exposed by the available raw-file interface; baseline public hashes and inspection date are recorded.",
    "Current athlete state, diagnosis/clinical instructions, recent training, thresholds, and live plan are private runtime inputs, not KB content.",
    "No study enrolled recreational runners who strength train and tested training adjustments around real flights; travel buffers and race-arrival nights are coaching conventions.",
    "No altitude-adaptation timeline is recorded: the IOC heat/altitude consensus text was not obtained and remains a candidate."
  ],
